Q: same size for elements in different containers in swiftui A: <p>When you apply <code>fixedSize</code> to a view, the view adopts its <em>ideal size</em>.</p>
<ul>
<li>In the case of an <code>Image</code>, the ideal size is the image with its natural proportions.</li>
<li>In the case of a <code>Color</code> or a <code>Shape</code>, the ideal size is very small (10x10).</li>
</ul>
<p>In your case, you have multiple containers with multiple items. To scale them all by the same amount, you can try applying <code>.scaledToFit()</code> to the outer container.</p>
<p>The following example shows this working for simple placeholder shapes (rounded rectangles). I don't quite know how the scaling algorithm works, but I found it was leaving excess space at the sides. By applying a <code>.scaleEffect</code> to the final result, you can make better use of the available space.</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>struct ContentView: View {
    var body: some View {
        HStack(spacing: 30) {
            KeyRows(nKeysInRow: [4, 4, 3, 3])
            KeyRows(nKeysInRow: [5, 5, 6, 5])
        }
        .scaledToFit()
        .scaleEffect(1 / 0.8)
    }
}

struct KeyRows: View {
    let nKeysInRow: [Int]

    var body: some View {
        VStack(spacing: 6) {
            ForEach(Array(nKeysInRow.enumerated()), id: \.offset) { _, n in
                HStack(spacing: 6) {
                    ForEach(0..&lt;n, id: \.self) { _ in
                        RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 6)
                            .fill(.gray.opacity(0.5))
                            .stroke(.gray)
                            .aspectRatio(0.8, contentMode: .fit)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/cWTRU9Kgm.png" alt="Screenshot" /></p>
<hr />
<p>When using images, I would suggest showing these as an overlay over a placeholder shape or color. To show it working, the example below uses <code>Color.clear</code> as the placeholder. 4 images with different proportions (named &quot;image1&quot; to &quot;image4&quot;) are shown at random over the placeholders:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>Color.clear
    .aspectRatio(0.8, contentMode: .fit)
    .overlay {
        Image(&quot;image\(Int.random(in: 1...4))&quot;)
            .resizable()
            .scaledToFit()
    }
    .clipShape(.rect(cornerRadius: 6))
    .overlay {
        RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 6)
            .stroke(.gray)
    }
</code></pre>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/0YNHnZCYm.png" alt="Screenshot" /></p>
